# Docket ships evidence, and evidence includes exact bytes.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) git rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That silently changed a published artefact: the Agent Advantage
# Report prints a minimal pair of payloads whose ONLY difference is a newline
# between two clauses, and a CRLF checkout turns the "\n" variant a reader
# copies into "\r\n" — a different string from the one that was actually
# tested and recorded. Forcing LF keeps the working tree, the object store,
# the served page and the committed experiment records byte-identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded experiments and their hashes are canonical JSON; never touch them. The v2
# corpus is hashed into its own pre-registration and that digest is cited by the run
# record, so a newline rewritten on checkout would break the citation rather than only the
# formatting — and the corpus carries a minimal pair whose whole content is one newline.
docket/advantage/experiments/*.json -text
docket/advantage/v2/corpus/*/*.json -text
docket/advantage/v2/specs/*.json -text
docket/advantage/v2/runs/*.json -text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
